  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This phone recording captures the Mountain Goats performing on Friday, February 17, 2023, at Musica in Akron, Ohio [1]. The setlist includes twenty songs, opening with “Going to Bogota” and “Dutch Orchestra Blues” before moving into “Color in Your Cheeks” and “Soft Targets” [1]. The band plays “Clemency for the Wizard King” and the rare “I Will Grab You by the Ears,” followed by “The Recognition Scene” and “Alpha Gelida” [1]. A notable moment occurs with “Love Cuts the Strings,” a bustout that had not appeared in 38 archived shows for 512 days [1]. The main set continues with “Southwestern Territory,” “Transcendental Youth,” “Hair Match,” and the rare “Mark On You” [1]. They close the main set with “First Blood,” “Cotton,” “Dance Music,” and “Up the Wolves” [1]. The encore features “Palmcorder Yajna,” “No Children,” and “This Year” [1]. The total runtime is 87 minutes [1]. The uploader notes that the audience was rather chatty during the performance [1]. This is the 363rd show in the archive’s collection for this performer [2]. The previous archived show took place on February 16, 2023, at Water Street Music Hall [2]. This recording is the only available capture of this specific date [1].",
